# Absolute path to the Silicon Altar audit repo.
# The shell READS from it and never writes to it.
#
# THERE IS NO DEFAULT. prepare-windows.mjs and prepare-corpus.mjs used to fall
# back to a hardcoded ~/Desktop/Silicon_Altar_LIVE; that path still exists and
# holds an abandoned, stale copy, so a missing line here built the wrong corpus
# instead of failing. Both scripts now refuse to run without this set.
#
# Use the ~/dev copy. Never a ~/Desktop copy.
SILICON_ALTAR_REPO=/Users/taylorcolin/dev/Silicon_Altar_LIVE

# The answering layer. Opus 5 through the official SDK; /api/ask holds this
# server-side and never ships it to the client.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Signs the sa_session cookie that middleware.ts verifies. Without it every
# request is rejected and nobody can sign in. Mint one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Rotating it invalidates every existing session immediately.
SESSION_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL. The operator's own invite code, so `npm run keepwarm` can sign in
# like anyone else. Printed once by `npm run invite -- --operator`.
# SA_INVITE_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL quota caps. Defaults are 25 per person per day, 60 across everyone,
# and 5 seconds between requests. See lib/quota.ts for the cost basis.
# BETA_DAILY_PER_PERSON=25
# BETA_DAILY_GLOBAL=60
# BETA_MIN_SECONDS_BETWEEN=5
